WEBVTT

00:02.628 --> 00:05.547
[♪♪♪]

00:05.631 --> 00:07.549
[wind whistling]

00:11.011 --> 00:16.140
1912 OTARU

00:19.978 --> 00:21.939
[woman]
Thank you for coming!

00:21.980 --> 00:24.149
SAKE

00:35.077 --> 00:36.787
Hey! What the...

00:36.828 --> 00:37.955
[woman]
Watch where you're going!

00:38.038 --> 00:39.081
The hell's your problem?

00:39.164 --> 00:42.125
Hold on.
Ain't you a fine woman?

00:42.209 --> 00:43.919
Get out of my way.

00:44.002 --> 00:46.463
A feisty one. My kind of woman.

00:47.464 --> 00:48.966
[grunts]

00:49.049 --> 00:50.926
What the hell
do you think you're...

00:51.009 --> 00:52.302
[grunts]

00:52.386 --> 00:53.512
[wheezes]

00:55.013 --> 00:58.767
What's it to you, old man?
You stay out of this!

01:00.018 --> 01:01.186
Huh?

01:06.817 --> 01:07.734
[scoffs]

01:09.152 --> 01:11.530
Hey, what the hell's
your problem, old man?

01:16.451 --> 01:18.078
[groaning]

01:22.541 --> 01:24.418
Forget it.
Let's get out of here!

01:24.501 --> 01:27.379
[man groans]

01:27.462 --> 01:28.672
Hey! Let's go!

01:28.755 --> 01:32.426
[woman] Impressive.
You haven't lost your touch.

01:33.884 --> 01:36.179
Nagakura Shinpachi...

01:37.222 --> 01:39.390
captain of the Shinsengumi's
second unit.

01:41.977 --> 01:44.271
And who are you?

01:45.146 --> 01:47.024
My name is Ichikawa Makoto.

01:47.065 --> 01:48.984
I've come from Tokyo.

01:49.067 --> 01:52.195
There's something
I must ask you.

01:54.448 --> 01:56.366
It's about the Shinsengumi.

01:56.450 --> 01:57.908
Leave!

01:57.993 --> 01:59.578
Please, wait.

01:59.661 --> 02:00.746
[Nagakura draws blade]

02:03.624 --> 02:05.584
I have nothing to say.

02:08.044 --> 02:10.213
I'm not leaving
until you talk to me.

02:11.590 --> 02:15.052
It can't be anyone else.
It has to be you.

02:15.093 --> 02:16.762
[blade draws]
[man yells]

02:17.763 --> 02:19.264
[grunting]

02:22.434 --> 02:23.685
[groans]

02:31.401 --> 02:32.694
You...

02:32.736 --> 02:36.073
You purposely let those drunks
harass you, didn't you?

02:36.156 --> 02:39.242
Please. I want to know
about the Shinsengumi...

02:40.118 --> 02:41.286
No...

02:43.079 --> 02:45.791
I need to know the truth
about Hijikata Toshizo.

02:47.125 --> 02:49.086
Hijikata Toshizo...

02:49.127 --> 02:52.297
[♪♪♪]

03:03.141 --> 03:04.309
He...

03:07.145 --> 03:09.314
had the same look in his eyes
as you.

03:15.195 --> 03:18.907
Prickly and aggressive,
like a briar patch.

03:18.990 --> 03:20.784
Or maybe reckless...

03:20.826 --> 03:21.827
EDO

03:21.910 --> 03:25.288
...like someone who'd charge

03:25.372 --> 03:28.291
right into one.

03:28.375 --> 03:29.918
You get hurt, I sell medicine.

03:30.001 --> 03:32.796
We called guys like that
baragaki, thorny brats.

03:34.131 --> 03:40.303
That was
Hijikata Toshizo to a T.

03:42.680 --> 03:43.932
Brace yourselves!

03:46.810 --> 03:48.603
[grunting]

03:49.187 --> 03:50.772
[laughs]

03:50.856 --> 03:52.315
Come on.

03:59.030 --> 04:00.907
[exclaiming]

04:11.626 --> 04:12.836
[yells fiercely]

04:13.712 --> 04:15.464
[screams]

04:18.675 --> 04:20.343
[yells fiercely]

04:20.427 --> 04:22.345
I'll be sure to get you
some medicine.

04:22.387 --> 04:24.264
[yells fiercely]

04:24.347 --> 04:25.682
[onlookers exclaim]

04:25.724 --> 04:28.143
[laughs]

04:28.226 --> 04:29.519
Master! Master!

04:29.603 --> 04:33.023
You! A low blow? You coward!

04:33.064 --> 04:34.316
Huh?

04:34.357 --> 04:37.444
The art of the sword
is for battles, isn't it?

04:37.527 --> 04:40.197
In battle, who gives a damn
about fighting fair?

04:40.238 --> 04:43.116
The gall of a mere merchant!

04:43.200 --> 04:44.784
Come on, bring it!

04:50.665 --> 04:52.584
Let me know
if you need more medicine!

04:55.587 --> 04:58.423
Hey, here.
Oh, thanks.

05:00.300 --> 05:02.552
Are you always pulling stunts
like this?

05:02.594 --> 05:05.138
Yep. It's quicker
to create the injured

05:05.222 --> 05:06.807
than to track them down.

05:07.974 --> 05:09.976
Right? There!

05:10.060 --> 05:12.646
Thanks for your business!
Don't ever come back!

05:12.729 --> 05:14.314
[laughing]

05:16.483 --> 05:19.945
What a face.
All right, my bad.

05:20.028 --> 05:22.823
[man] Just get out already!
Yeah, yeah, I'm going.

05:24.449 --> 05:26.243
[kids shouting playfully]

05:26.284 --> 05:28.245
[indistinct singing]

05:28.286 --> 05:30.455
[people chattering indistinctly]

05:35.210 --> 05:37.087
[wind blowing]

05:51.810 --> 05:54.604
The Shieikan dojo.

06:03.488 --> 06:04.781
What a dump...

06:09.578 --> 06:13.164
Hey. This is a dojo, right?

06:17.794 --> 06:20.672
Hyah!
Hyah!

06:20.755 --> 06:22.674
Come on! Knock it off!
You little bastards!

06:23.633 --> 06:25.051
You're supposed to fall.

06:25.135 --> 06:26.845
Huh?

06:26.928 --> 06:28.013
Because they cut you.

06:28.096 --> 06:30.015
[Nagakura]
Okita Soji.

06:30.098 --> 06:31.850
Though normally gentle

06:31.933 --> 06:35.145
once he draws his sword,
he's a demon

06:35.186 --> 06:37.314
a true sword-fighting prodigy.

06:37.397 --> 06:39.482
Hyah!
Hyah!

06:39.524 --> 06:42.152
[groaning]
A surprise attack... Well done.

06:42.235 --> 06:43.570
That means I win.

06:43.653 --> 06:46.114
I'm the one who cut down
our master. I won.

06:46.156 --> 06:48.199
[Abiru] Now. I believe I said
no fighting, didn't I?

06:48.283 --> 06:49.492
You two are friends, right?

06:49.576 --> 06:52.329
[Nagakura]
Abiru Eisaburo.

06:52.412 --> 06:53.955
He's a bit timid,

06:53.997 --> 06:57.292
but that kindness is the
conscience of Shieikan Dojo.

06:57.375 --> 06:58.501
Okay, good boy.

07:00.086 --> 07:02.339
Soji! Eisaburo! Food's ready.

07:02.380 --> 07:03.506
NAGAKURA SHINPACHI

07:03.548 --> 07:06.343
Don't mind me.

07:06.426 --> 07:08.261
Let's go. Okay?

07:08.345 --> 07:10.096
I'm starving!

07:10.180 --> 07:14.017
[Nagakura] Sanosuke! Hajime!
Heisuke! Hurry up and eat.

07:18.438 --> 07:19.773
What's this?

07:19.856 --> 07:21.149
Harada Sanosuke.

07:21.232 --> 07:22.567
HARADA SANOSUKE

07:22.651 --> 07:25.111
He loves his food
more than anything,

07:25.195 --> 07:27.864
and can't stand pointless talk.

07:27.948 --> 07:29.032
Man, this is good.

07:30.450 --> 07:32.911
Greens again?
We're pinching pennies, huh?

07:34.537 --> 07:37.666
If you don't want it,
can we give yours to the kids?

07:37.749 --> 07:39.042
They're still growing.

07:39.084 --> 07:40.710
Fine. They can have it.

07:40.794 --> 07:42.420
[Nagakura]
I've never known anyone

07:42.504 --> 07:45.131
who could wield
a sword as masterfully as him.

07:45.215 --> 07:48.593
That's Saito Hajime.

07:50.679 --> 07:52.347
Then you can have
some of mine too.

07:52.430 --> 07:53.640
Really? Thanks.

07:53.723 --> 07:55.141
[Nagakura]
Todo Heisuke.

07:55.225 --> 07:56.558
TODO HEISUKE

07:56.643 --> 07:58.561
He's the kindest person
you'll ever meet,

07:58.645 --> 08:00.563
but he's also
quick to pick a fight.

08:00.605 --> 08:02.399
[crunches]
[gasps]

08:02.482 --> 08:04.401
Are you kidding me?

08:04.442 --> 08:05.735
[laughing]

08:05.777 --> 08:07.904
[Nagakura]
Yamanami Keisuke

08:07.946 --> 08:11.241
is the most logical
of all at Shieikan.

08:11.282 --> 08:13.910
Don't go wild at mealtime!

08:13.994 --> 08:17.205
[♪♪♪]

08:17.288 --> 08:18.873
Gen, wake up. It's time to eat.

08:18.915 --> 08:21.418
[Nagakura] The eldest of us,
Inoue Genzaburo...

08:21.501 --> 08:22.544
Wake up! Hey!

08:22.627 --> 08:23.628
INOUE GENZABURO

08:23.712 --> 08:26.548
...is always asleep. Yep.

08:27.799 --> 08:29.968
This'll be an easy win.

08:32.095 --> 08:33.138
And who might you be?

08:34.639 --> 08:36.890
Sorry to interrupt your meal.

08:36.975 --> 08:38.684
I'm a traveling
medicine salesman.

08:38.768 --> 08:40.937
You folks need anything?

08:45.483 --> 08:47.402
We don't need any!
Get outta here!

08:47.485 --> 08:48.903
[exclaims softly]

08:48.987 --> 08:51.906
They say
"Better safe than sorry."

08:51.990 --> 08:54.993
Or have you never heard
that one?

08:57.078 --> 08:58.121
What's your problem?

09:00.248 --> 09:02.042
I'm here to challenge your dojo!

09:02.125 --> 09:04.169
[rooster crows]

09:04.252 --> 09:05.628
Master of the dojo!

09:07.088 --> 09:08.590
Come out!

09:11.217 --> 09:14.179
[Nagakura] And the man
who'd become the fourth master

09:14.262 --> 09:15.930
of the Tennen Rishin-ryu style

09:15.972 --> 09:18.600
if you think of Shieikan
as one big family,

09:18.683 --> 09:20.268
he would be its father.

09:20.351 --> 09:21.895
Boss.

09:21.978 --> 09:28.485
A man worthy of the title,
Kondo Isami.

09:28.526 --> 09:31.863
[Nagakura] Boss.
We've got a strange visitor.

09:31.946 --> 09:33.156
Hmm?

09:33.239 --> 09:34.491
KONDO ISAMI

09:34.574 --> 09:36.493
Can't it wait?

09:36.576 --> 09:37.827
[Nagakura] Hurry.

09:37.869 --> 09:39.412
[Kondo]
What's all the fuss?

09:39.496 --> 09:41.414
[Nagakura]
This guy's got some nerve.

09:41.498 --> 09:43.875
He's got some nerve?
That's him. Right there.

09:50.924 --> 09:52.801
You wouldn't happen to be...

09:52.884 --> 09:54.969
the medicine peddler
I've heard about,

09:55.053 --> 09:57.680
who's been crushing dojos
all over Kanto?

10:00.558 --> 10:01.684
What if I am?

10:04.479 --> 10:08.108
Word is you're a real handful.

10:08.191 --> 10:10.026
Ehh?

10:11.653 --> 10:14.197
[♪♪♪]

10:23.164 --> 10:24.374
Your name?

10:26.584 --> 10:28.044
From Ishida Village in Tama.

10:30.630 --> 10:32.173
Hijikata Toshizo.

10:47.480 --> 10:49.107
Hmm?

10:49.190 --> 10:50.275
What's the matter?

10:51.609 --> 10:53.778
In a real fight, you'd be dead.

10:56.072 --> 10:58.116
[both grunting]

11:22.140 --> 11:24.100
[panting]

11:41.951 --> 11:43.369
Too much wasted movement.

11:43.453 --> 11:45.830
Don't you dare talk down to me!

11:53.504 --> 11:55.256
[chuckling]

11:55.340 --> 11:56.382
[shouts]

12:19.822 --> 12:22.867
That won't get you very far
in a real battle.

12:22.951 --> 12:24.285
This is how you kick.

12:25.578 --> 12:26.537
[grunts]

12:30.541 --> 12:32.377
[laughing]

12:32.460 --> 12:36.005
Ouch. Boss doesn't hold back.
You think that guy's okay?

12:36.047 --> 12:37.966
[coughing]

12:42.303 --> 12:43.888
You're good!

12:45.640 --> 12:47.016
Finally, after all this time...

12:47.100 --> 12:48.935
Someone who can make me
stronger.

12:52.021 --> 12:54.524
If we go on,
this could turn deadly.

12:54.565 --> 12:55.858
[pants]

12:58.236 --> 13:00.822
If I'm not strong enough,
I'll die.

13:00.905 --> 13:02.907
That's all there is to it.

13:04.951 --> 13:07.370
Why are you so desperate
to become stronger?

13:10.832 --> 13:12.000
It's my blood.

13:13.584 --> 13:14.961
[Kondo]
Your blood?

13:16.754 --> 13:18.881
I can't stop my blood
from boiling.

13:21.843 --> 13:24.095
Only when I'm fighting
someone strong...

13:25.930 --> 13:28.099
do I truly feel alive.

13:31.811 --> 13:33.187
In this day and age...

13:34.772 --> 13:37.233
swordsmanship is obsolete.

13:37.317 --> 13:38.234
[panting]

13:38.276 --> 13:40.236
No matter how strong
your sword is,

13:40.278 --> 13:42.405
you can't change
this country's course.

13:45.742 --> 13:47.118
Are you an idiot?

13:49.829 --> 13:53.958
What's the fun in doing
the sensible thing?

13:57.128 --> 14:02.383
Doing what no one else can
is what makes you a badass.

14:22.528 --> 14:23.988
[chuckles softly]

14:25.865 --> 14:28.409
[♪♪♪]

14:31.371 --> 14:32.580
[sighs]

14:34.790 --> 14:36.000
I agree.

14:38.336 --> 14:39.337
My apologies.

14:45.134 --> 14:47.428
If that is so,
then I will give it my all.

14:49.389 --> 14:50.348
Yeah!

15:02.735 --> 15:05.154
[grunting]

15:07.907 --> 15:09.367
Don't die on me!

15:10.868 --> 15:12.161
Wait a second!

15:22.505 --> 15:24.090
[groaning]

15:36.561 --> 15:37.520
Aah!

15:45.528 --> 15:46.571
Gotcha!

15:49.407 --> 15:50.658
Not good enough.

15:55.329 --> 15:56.664
[Todo laughing]

15:59.125 --> 16:00.460
He's okay, right?

16:01.836 --> 16:03.671
[Saito]
I'm sure he's not dead.

16:05.923 --> 16:07.091
Hey, hey.

16:10.178 --> 16:11.095
Hey.

16:13.264 --> 16:15.099
He's laughing
while he's unconscious.

16:15.183 --> 16:17.477
You're right.
That's creepy.

16:19.103 --> 16:21.689
He gave you a tougher time
than expected, didn't he?

16:21.731 --> 16:23.441
It's been a while
since I've seen you

16:23.524 --> 16:25.735
get that serious, Kondo.

16:25.776 --> 16:27.487
Hey.

16:27.570 --> 16:30.239
[Kondo] Yeah, I didn't think
he had it in him.

16:30.323 --> 16:34.452
This guy... he might be
a good fit for us.

16:37.121 --> 16:39.165
[Nagakura]
Tennen Rishin-ryu.

16:39.248 --> 16:41.792
A style built
for a battle to the death

16:41.876 --> 16:43.461
a practical combat style

16:43.544 --> 16:46.631
that requires facing your foe
with complete abandon.

16:46.714 --> 16:47.924
Pretty good, huh?

16:47.965 --> 16:49.467
[crunching]

16:54.305 --> 16:55.515
Hm.

16:55.598 --> 16:56.641
[Abiru] Here.

16:56.724 --> 16:59.602
[Nagakura]
In spring 1859

16:59.644 --> 17:02.188
Hijikata Toshizo joined

17:02.271 --> 17:06.776
the Tennen Rishin-ryu's
Shieikan dojo.

17:06.858 --> 17:09.194
Age 24.

17:10.988 --> 17:12.531
There.

17:14.200 --> 17:15.742
[♪♪♪]

17:15.785 --> 17:20.248
It was four years
before the Shinsengumi's name

17:20.330 --> 17:22.040
would echo through Kyoto.

17:22.124 --> 17:26.295
[♪♪♪]

17:33.094 --> 17:40.184
SONG OF THE SAMURAI

17:49.694 --> 17:52.947
[Nagakura] At the time,
the shogunate's real power

17:52.989 --> 17:55.950
was held by the Great Elder,
Ii Naosuke.

17:56.033 --> 17:58.703
Ever since
the Black Ships arrived,

17:58.786 --> 18:01.330
he strongly advocated
for opening Japan.

18:01.414 --> 18:03.124
If we go to war with America,

18:03.207 --> 18:05.293
our country stands
no chance of winning.

18:06.502 --> 18:08.588
Even if we cannot obtain
an imperial sanction

18:08.671 --> 18:11.549
we have no other choice
but to sign the treaty!

18:11.632 --> 18:16.345
[Nagakura]
However, on March 24, 1860

18:16.429 --> 18:18.973
he was killed by ronin
from Mito

18:19.056 --> 18:21.559
outside of
the Sakuradamon Gate.

18:23.060 --> 18:26.230
Following this,
the pro-opening shogunate

18:26.314 --> 18:29.275
and the opposing
Sonno Joi faction...

18:30.693 --> 18:33.029
were plunged into
an all-out confrontation.

18:33.112 --> 18:35.448
[sword slices]
[cries out]

18:35.531 --> 18:36.782
TENNEN RISHIN-RYU SHIEIKAN DOJO

18:36.866 --> 18:38.743
[Todo]
Now's your chance! Go!

18:38.826 --> 18:41.287
I humbly beg for your pardon.

18:41.370 --> 18:43.831
I humbly beg for your pardon!

18:43.914 --> 18:46.125
I humbly beg your pardon.

18:46.208 --> 18:47.877
[kids shouting]

18:47.960 --> 18:49.378
I humbly beg your pardon.

18:51.088 --> 18:52.882
Ouch!

18:52.965 --> 18:54.550
Stop!

18:56.052 --> 18:59.055
[groans]

18:59.138 --> 19:02.099
Naosuke the perv,
we took your head!

19:02.183 --> 19:04.060
Naosuke the perv!
Naosuke the perv!

19:04.143 --> 19:07.063
It's Naosuke. It's Naosuke!

19:07.104 --> 19:08.397
Ii Naosuke. Ke!

19:08.481 --> 19:10.524
[kids] Naosuke the perv!
The perv!

19:10.608 --> 19:13.361
998.

19:18.115 --> 19:20.201
999.

19:24.997 --> 19:26.415
1,000!

19:28.959 --> 19:30.878
[chickens clucking]

19:36.217 --> 19:37.718
Hey, Soji.

19:37.802 --> 19:39.303
Yes?

19:40.471 --> 19:41.847
It's been a whole year!

19:43.224 --> 19:44.642
A thousand practice swings.

19:45.893 --> 19:50.272
Every single day, without fail.

19:50.356 --> 19:52.316
Haven't I done enough?

19:53.275 --> 19:55.027
Teach me a move or something!

19:55.111 --> 19:56.362
An actual technique!

19:56.445 --> 19:59.407
If you can complain,
you can swing.

19:59.448 --> 20:00.408
Shut up!

20:02.368 --> 20:03.536
How am I supposed
to beat our boss

20:03.619 --> 20:05.329
with just practice swings?
Huh?

20:05.413 --> 20:08.165
The whole reason I joined
was to beat him!

20:08.249 --> 20:09.917
Beat the boss, you say?

20:11.293 --> 20:13.337
Not in a hundred years!
[Okita] All right.

20:14.338 --> 20:16.257
I'll teach you
a special technique.

20:16.340 --> 20:18.342
Soji...
But only if...

20:19.218 --> 20:20.594
you can beat me.

20:22.722 --> 20:24.640
You're on.

20:24.724 --> 20:26.058
Get me a wooden sword!

20:26.142 --> 20:27.643
I'm gonna beat the hell
out of you.

20:27.685 --> 20:28.936
I'm fine with this.

20:29.019 --> 20:30.354
Huh?!

20:32.148 --> 20:33.524
Don't you mock me.

20:38.863 --> 20:41.907
[♪♪♪]

20:47.913 --> 20:50.249
[laughing]

20:51.250 --> 20:52.793
Mmm...

20:52.877 --> 20:53.961
This is good.

20:56.464 --> 20:57.882
Ouch. My stomach hurts.

20:57.965 --> 20:59.675
You're laughing too hard.

20:59.717 --> 21:03.679
Come on, this guy
spent a whole year

21:03.763 --> 21:07.391
doing a thousand practice swings
every single day

21:07.475 --> 21:10.186
and he couldn't land
a single hit on him.

21:10.227 --> 21:11.520
And to top it all off,

21:11.604 --> 21:14.023
he got his ass kicked
with a futon beater!

21:14.064 --> 21:17.193
Basically,
that makes you a futon!

21:17.276 --> 21:19.236
A futon!

21:19.320 --> 21:20.738
Well said indeed.

21:20.821 --> 21:24.742
Don't get cocky.
Our match begins now, Hajime!

21:24.825 --> 21:27.536
Lose to me
and you've lost to a futon.

21:27.578 --> 21:29.371
I'll take you on!
You flat futon!

21:29.413 --> 21:30.706
Who you calling flat futon!

21:30.748 --> 21:32.249
[Abiru]
Hey, you two, no fighting!

21:32.333 --> 21:34.084
[Nagakura]
Knock it off! We're eating now.

21:34.168 --> 21:35.544
Let them be. Let them be.

21:35.586 --> 21:38.172
Food and fighting.
Just like a family!

21:38.255 --> 21:42.259
Toshi! Hajime!
Stop it already.

21:42.343 --> 21:43.594
Hey, get off me.

21:46.764 --> 21:50.518
Kondo, you're the master
of this dojo.

21:50.601 --> 21:52.686
You should have
more dignity.

21:56.774 --> 21:59.401
Nameless patriots
changed history

21:59.485 --> 22:01.570
at the Sakuradamon Incident.

22:01.612 --> 22:03.113
Doesn't that frustrate you?

22:04.657 --> 22:07.493
I wish we'd hear back
about the Kobusho.

22:08.994 --> 22:10.496
The Kobusho?

22:10.579 --> 22:14.500
Still no word, I'm afraid.

22:14.583 --> 22:17.711
Oh man, don't remind me.

22:19.380 --> 22:22.758
Hey, what is the Kobusho,
anyway?

22:22.800 --> 22:25.427
It's the shogunate's official
military academy.

22:25.469 --> 22:28.347
Things have been turbulent
since the Black Ships arrived.

22:28.430 --> 22:29.974
To prepare for the worst

22:30.057 --> 22:33.018
the shogunate established it to
bolster their military forces.

22:33.102 --> 22:35.187
[Nagakura] They teach
swordsmanship, spearmanship

22:35.271 --> 22:37.189
and even Western-style
artillery.

22:37.273 --> 22:39.733
The instructors are
the best of the best,

22:39.817 --> 22:42.319
brought in from
all across the country.

22:42.403 --> 22:45.489
So it's the ultimate
training center,

22:45.573 --> 22:48.617
taught by the strongest guys
around.

22:48.701 --> 22:50.578
[Okita] Kondo is currently
running himself ragged

22:50.619 --> 22:52.997
trying to become
one of those instructors.

22:53.080 --> 22:57.877
The instructors are first-class,
sanctioned by the shogunate.

22:57.960 --> 23:01.922
Then Shieikan's name
would be recognized as well.

23:02.006 --> 23:07.303
We'll get a stipend and we can
finally get out of this dump!

23:07.386 --> 23:10.556
And we could teach
so many more kids.

23:10.639 --> 23:13.851
That should be a piece of cake
with your skills, Boss.

23:15.686 --> 23:19.940
[Yamanami]
No, it's not quite that simple.

23:20.024 --> 23:22.151
[Hijikata]
Huh? What do you mean by that?

23:25.362 --> 23:26.405
[sets down chopsticks]

23:26.488 --> 23:28.908
Either way at this rate,

23:28.991 --> 23:32.369
the Shieikan will always be
just a beat-up old dojo.

23:32.453 --> 23:33.704
Making a name for ourselves

23:33.787 --> 23:35.956
will be nothing more
than a pipe dream.

23:40.127 --> 23:41.712
[Inoue] Hm.

23:45.966 --> 23:46.884
What's this?

23:48.928 --> 23:50.971
[Okita] Is that about
the crossroads slasher?

23:52.431 --> 23:55.351
Oh, the one
who's been popping up lately?

23:55.434 --> 23:58.771
Yeah. There was one
about three days ago too...

24:04.318 --> 24:05.861
A wooden sword...

24:05.903 --> 24:08.948
You think you can challenge me
with that?

24:10.366 --> 24:13.369
Don't mess with me,
you worthless punk!

24:13.452 --> 24:14.370
[blow thwacks]

24:14.453 --> 24:17.247
[groaning]

24:17.331 --> 24:20.084
He took down Watanabe Noboru,
who had a real sword, head-on

24:20.167 --> 24:22.294
with just a wooden sword?

24:22.378 --> 24:25.172
Is this Watanabe guy any good?

24:25.255 --> 24:29.093
He's the head instructor of
the Shindo Munen-ryu Renpeikan

24:29.176 --> 24:30.469
one of Edo's top three dojos.

24:30.552 --> 24:33.055
To face a master
with a wooden sword,

24:33.097 --> 24:34.932
he must be incredibly confident.

24:35.015 --> 24:36.767
WANTED

24:37.559 --> 24:38.769
All right.

24:39.895 --> 24:41.814
If I take down
this slasher bastard,

24:41.897 --> 24:44.608
it'll make a name
for the Shieikan.

24:47.403 --> 24:48.612
Hm.

24:50.197 --> 24:51.115
Interesting.

24:52.533 --> 24:53.659
All right, I'll do it.

24:53.742 --> 24:55.786
Listen to Mr. Flat futon. Moron!

24:55.869 --> 24:57.579
[Okita] I agree.
I don't think you can do it.

24:57.663 --> 24:59.248
The way you are now, Hijikata,

24:59.289 --> 25:01.250
you couldn't win
in a hundred tries.

25:01.333 --> 25:03.919
Soji, you too, you bastard!

25:04.003 --> 25:05.045
That hurt!

25:05.129 --> 25:07.673
[cackling]

25:07.756 --> 25:10.676
That's enough out of all of you!
Hey!

25:11.844 --> 25:14.805
Flat futon! That bastard Saito!

25:16.640 --> 25:20.144
And I'm gonna crush Soji
one of these days.

25:20.227 --> 25:21.937
I'll take them all down...

25:22.021 --> 25:24.189
You are to take down
the crossroads slasher, right?

25:26.316 --> 25:28.110
Boss...

25:28.193 --> 25:29.236
I'll go with you.

25:30.320 --> 25:31.572
What?

25:31.655 --> 25:34.450
If you've just come to mock me,
forget it.

25:34.491 --> 25:36.452
Don't sulk.

25:36.535 --> 25:39.788
So? What's your plan
for finding this slasher?

25:39.872 --> 25:42.499
You're not just going
to wander all night

25:42.583 --> 25:44.418
hoping he'll jump you, are you?

25:44.501 --> 25:46.670
[laughing]

25:47.671 --> 25:49.840
I've got a plan for that.

25:51.008 --> 25:53.969
[♪♪♪]

25:57.598 --> 25:58.766
That's him.

26:00.059 --> 26:03.353
What makes you think
he'll be the next target?

26:03.437 --> 26:06.065
Kashiwai Shunsuke
is a master of iai, right?

26:06.148 --> 26:10.402
That slasher bastard, he's never
fought an iai master, right?

26:10.486 --> 26:11.695
I see.

26:12.654 --> 26:14.698
Pretty clever, Toshi...
for you.

26:14.782 --> 26:16.075
Don't be a smartass.

26:25.250 --> 26:27.211
[wind whistling]

26:33.884 --> 26:34.802
What?

26:36.220 --> 26:39.139
[♪♪♪]

27:00.577 --> 27:02.287
[Okadaizo]
You wouldn't happen to be

27:02.371 --> 27:03.872
Kashiwai Shunsuke, would you?

27:05.040 --> 27:06.041
That I am.

27:09.586 --> 27:10.879
I request...

27:12.589 --> 27:14.216
the honor of a match.

27:16.510 --> 27:17.761
That's him.

27:22.891 --> 27:25.269
I've been waiting for you,
crossroads slasher.

27:27.229 --> 27:29.064
[Kashiwai's aide screaming]

27:30.440 --> 27:32.401
Toshi!

27:32.442 --> 27:33.902
Come! I'll drown you in blood--

27:33.986 --> 27:37.072
You damn crossroads slasher!

27:39.658 --> 27:42.244
I'm Hijikata Toshizo
of Tennen Rishin-ryu!

27:43.912 --> 27:45.247
And who the hell are you?

27:48.292 --> 27:49.668
Okada Izo.

27:50.961 --> 27:51.879
[scoffing]

27:51.962 --> 27:54.715
You're a crossroads slasher

27:54.756 --> 27:56.633
and you're just gonna give me
your name that easily?

27:56.717 --> 27:58.677
Ah! Oh!

27:58.760 --> 28:01.054
It just slipped out. Crap!

28:01.889 --> 28:03.849
Oh. You from Tosa?

28:05.392 --> 28:07.102
How could you tell?

28:07.186 --> 28:10.564
Ha-ha! Your thick Tosa accent
gives you away. What? Come on!

28:10.647 --> 28:11.732
[groaning]

28:11.815 --> 28:13.734
What is with this guy?

28:13.817 --> 28:16.820
Why you... Okada Izo!
Brace yourself!

28:21.241 --> 28:23.827
If you come at me all of
a sudden, I can't hold back.

28:24.703 --> 28:25.829
What a speed...

28:25.913 --> 28:27.831
The guy's a monster.

28:28.790 --> 28:31.293
Feel free to run
if you want.

28:31.376 --> 28:32.878
Run away?

28:34.713 --> 28:36.423
You can talk trash
after you've beaten me,

28:36.506 --> 28:37.841
the strongest man
in all of Edo.

28:39.176 --> 28:40.219
The strongest?

28:41.803 --> 28:43.138
You're the strongest?

28:44.181 --> 28:45.224
That's right.

28:47.476 --> 28:51.146
If you claim to be
the strongest man in Edo...

28:51.188 --> 28:52.439
OKADA IZO

28:52.481 --> 28:55.192
...then I just have to beat you
to be the new strongest.

28:58.779 --> 29:00.989
Hey, you! The big guy!

29:01.990 --> 29:03.784
Huh? Me?

29:03.867 --> 29:07.120
That sword you have at your hip.
Give it to this man.

29:09.081 --> 29:11.625
I don't want him complaining
that he lost

29:11.708 --> 29:13.919
because he didn't have
a real blade.

29:16.713 --> 29:18.882
Don't you dare look down on me.

29:19.925 --> 29:23.011
If you're using a wooden sword,
so am I.

29:24.805 --> 29:28.267
Is that right?
Suit yourself.

29:28.350 --> 29:32.354
[♪♪♪]

29:32.396 --> 29:34.356
[both grunting]

29:41.029 --> 29:42.030
[grunts]

29:46.743 --> 29:49.246
[coughing]

29:49.329 --> 29:53.250
What, are you all talk?

29:57.337 --> 29:58.922
Too close, too close.

30:01.466 --> 30:02.551
Huh?

30:08.807 --> 30:11.852
[laughing]

30:15.647 --> 30:17.274
Unbelievable!

30:18.608 --> 30:20.110
[yells fiercely]

30:22.529 --> 30:25.490
[both straining]

31:11.328 --> 31:14.247
[♪♪♪]

31:37.270 --> 31:38.355
[yells fiercely]

31:44.653 --> 31:46.363
They're evenly matched.

31:48.407 --> 31:50.075
[straining]

32:05.882 --> 32:07.008
Unh!

32:14.057 --> 32:16.226
See? I'm the strongest one here!

32:22.315 --> 32:25.569
No... I am.

32:27.112 --> 32:31.533
Hey, Toshi! Toshi! Toshi!

32:31.575 --> 32:33.535
[fire crackling]

32:41.084 --> 32:43.587
You're pretty damn good.

32:45.797 --> 32:47.757
You've got some skills yourself.

32:48.925 --> 32:50.385
Still, why are you out here

32:50.427 --> 32:52.679
slashing people
with a wooden sword?

32:52.762 --> 32:54.514
Oh?

32:54.598 --> 32:58.268
This way, I don't
actually kill my opponents.

32:58.351 --> 33:01.396
And that means I can fight
strong guys over and over.

33:01.480 --> 33:05.734
But... if you get cut down,
it's over.

33:06.610 --> 33:07.986
Oh!

33:08.945 --> 33:10.489
[Okada gasps]
Didn't it...

33:11.615 --> 33:12.699
ever occur to you

33:12.782 --> 33:14.618
that you could be the one
to lose?

33:15.577 --> 33:16.495
No.

33:17.913 --> 33:22.751
But...
I don't like killing people.

33:22.834 --> 33:25.003
[laughing]

33:28.423 --> 33:30.592
[laughing]

33:30.634 --> 33:32.636
[laughing]

33:36.139 --> 33:41.311
Then why are you doing
this whole slasher thing anyway?

33:47.108 --> 33:48.318
To become...

33:49.611 --> 33:51.196
the strongest man there is.

33:56.660 --> 33:58.203
Oh...

33:59.663 --> 34:00.705
What a coincidence.

34:02.958 --> 34:04.209
Same here.

34:12.132 --> 34:15.303
We'll have another match,
Toshizo.

34:19.349 --> 34:20.391
Sure.

34:21.768 --> 34:24.688
[♪♪♪]

34:33.655 --> 34:35.824
[sneezes]
[sneezes]

34:35.864 --> 34:37.826
[fierce grunting in background]

34:42.371 --> 34:44.748
[Nagakura]
I still can't believe it!

34:44.833 --> 34:49.379
Toshi! You really fought that
crossroad slasher to a draw?

34:49.462 --> 34:51.630
How many times must I tell you?
Yes.

34:51.715 --> 34:53.882
Drop the empty bravado.

34:53.967 --> 34:55.844
That's pretty petty.

34:55.927 --> 34:59.097
Your comrade went toe-to-toe
with a seriously tough guy.

34:59.180 --> 35:01.391
The least we can do
is give him credit for it.

35:02.559 --> 35:06.313
So, where's the crossroad
slasher now?

35:08.064 --> 35:09.482
Who knows?

35:09.566 --> 35:10.900
We said,
"We'll have another match,"

35:10.984 --> 35:12.027
and went our separate ways.

35:12.068 --> 35:13.903
Huh?

35:13.987 --> 35:15.530
What were you thinking?

35:15.572 --> 35:18.408
You found the slasher
and just let him go?

35:18.491 --> 35:19.534
Because...

35:23.204 --> 35:25.540
...he was a hell of a guy.

35:25.582 --> 35:29.878
[♪♪♪]

35:29.961 --> 35:31.796
I know!

35:31.880 --> 35:33.882
Why don't we have him
join us?

35:33.965 --> 35:35.216
With someone that strong,

35:35.258 --> 35:36.885
the Shieikan's name
would spread fast.

35:36.968 --> 35:38.178
Wait, didn't you go fight him

35:38.261 --> 35:39.888
to boost our name
in the first place?

35:41.681 --> 35:42.766
Oh, right.

35:43.975 --> 35:45.268
[Hijikata chuckles]

35:46.936 --> 35:52.484
Boss, did he really fight
that slasher to a standstill?

35:54.361 --> 35:56.237
You still don't believe it?

35:56.321 --> 36:00.200
[Nagakura]
It was just yesterday that Toshi

36:00.283 --> 36:01.910
couldn't score a single point

36:01.951 --> 36:03.745
against Soji
with a futon beater.

36:05.163 --> 36:06.289
That's true.

36:07.624 --> 36:11.544
At first, the slasher
had the upper hand. But...

36:12.962 --> 36:15.256
gradually,
it became an even fight.

36:16.633 --> 36:17.801
Toshi's sword...

36:20.136 --> 36:23.890
may show its true worth
only at the limit.

36:28.478 --> 36:32.524
That man... he might be
deeper than he seems.

36:44.202 --> 36:45.787
[sword slashes]

36:51.543 --> 36:54.254
[whimpering]

37:13.690 --> 37:15.817
[student]
Oh, the Hiraseigan stance.

37:19.195 --> 37:21.030
[grunting]

37:21.114 --> 37:22.198
[groans]

37:22.282 --> 37:24.242
Damn it, I was so close...

37:24.325 --> 37:26.536
No, you're mistaken.
You were wide open.

37:26.619 --> 37:28.538
Yeah, I know.

37:28.621 --> 37:31.791
Your impatience is hindering
your progress.

37:31.875 --> 37:34.961
Hiraseigan is a dangerous stance
that risks a mutual strike.

37:35.044 --> 37:36.629
Don't rush yourself.

37:40.717 --> 37:42.427
I know, but...

37:58.401 --> 38:00.278
What's up, Eisaburo?

38:00.361 --> 38:03.448
You're practicing
the Hiraseigan stance, too?

38:04.574 --> 38:08.119
Hm. I want to master it, too.

38:08.203 --> 38:10.622
Then have Soji teach you.

38:10.705 --> 38:13.541
I already asked him,
but he said no.

38:13.625 --> 38:15.502
How come?

38:17.170 --> 38:19.756
He said the Hiraseigan
is too dangerous.

38:19.839 --> 38:24.135
Soji only teaches it
to those the Boss approves of.

38:24.219 --> 38:26.471
That's why
I'll master it myself.

38:30.391 --> 38:32.727
Then have him teach you
a different technique.

38:34.145 --> 38:35.480
No,

38:36.356 --> 38:37.816
it has to be the Hiraseigan.

38:39.901 --> 38:41.569
What do you mean by that?

38:45.156 --> 38:47.742
Because losing
is not an option.

38:56.292 --> 38:58.336
Got someone
you're dying to take down?

39:26.114 --> 39:27.574
Aim!

39:27.657 --> 39:29.284
THE SHOGUNATE KOBUSHO IN EDO

39:29.367 --> 39:31.369
Please!

39:31.452 --> 39:32.704
I beg you...

39:34.289 --> 39:36.624
please reconsider one more time.

39:36.666 --> 39:38.918
I believe I have told you
before.

39:39.002 --> 39:43.548
A farmer's backwater sword style
has no place in our Kobusho.

39:45.425 --> 39:48.136
However many times you come,
my answer won't change!

39:48.219 --> 39:49.888
With all due respect!

39:53.641 --> 39:58.146
Our Tennen Rishin-ryu style
has a proven track record.

39:59.272 --> 40:00.940
A track record?
Yes.

40:02.984 --> 40:04.986
The Nikko Toshogu Shrine,

40:05.028 --> 40:07.488
where the divine Lord Ieyasu
is enshrined.

40:07.572 --> 40:10.825
Among the Hachioji Sennin Doshin
who serve as its guards

40:10.867 --> 40:14.787
are a great number of
Tennen Rishin-ryu practitioners.

40:14.871 --> 40:21.502
Furthermore, in the registry
by Sanada Hannosuke

40:21.544 --> 40:23.588
head of the Hokushin
Itto-ryu Genbukan

40:23.671 --> 40:26.758
out of the 633
martial artists listed,

40:26.841 --> 40:30.511
64 are from
our Tennen Rishin-ryu.

40:30.553 --> 40:33.681
Among the 21 schools
in the registry,

40:33.765 --> 40:36.893
ours is the third-most
represented.

40:38.102 --> 40:40.188
Besides, the Kobusho...

40:40.229 --> 40:41.689
was established by the shogunate

40:41.773 --> 40:43.900
to boost its military power,
was it not?

40:46.778 --> 40:49.614
Then there is no style
more fitting

40:49.697 --> 40:51.532
than our Tennen Rishin-ryu

40:51.574 --> 40:53.952
perfected for actual battle.

41:02.335 --> 41:03.711
[slurps]

41:03.753 --> 41:05.213
Ah!

41:05.296 --> 41:07.799
Thank you so much, Yamanami!

41:09.634 --> 41:11.970
I can finally become
an official instructors!

41:12.053 --> 41:13.221
[all laugh]

41:13.262 --> 41:14.639
Congratulations.

41:14.722 --> 41:16.057
You're finally retainers,
just as you dreamed.

41:16.099 --> 41:19.060
This will make a name
for the Shieikan dojo.

41:19.143 --> 41:21.688
So long, poverty!

41:21.771 --> 41:23.564
We can buy the kids
new bamboo swords.

41:23.648 --> 41:26.401
And we'll get more food
on the table!

41:26.484 --> 41:28.277
Let's not
get ahead of ourselves.

41:28.361 --> 41:30.279
Nothing's official yet.

41:30.363 --> 41:31.739
That may be true,

41:31.823 --> 41:34.200
but we did receive
an unofficial offer.

41:36.661 --> 41:37.954
More than anything

41:39.622 --> 41:41.749
your words truly moved me,
Yamanami.

41:45.962 --> 41:48.089
Getting our hopes up
is a mistake.

41:48.172 --> 41:51.092
It always has been--
[Hijikata] Come on, Yamanami.

41:51.134 --> 41:52.593
Just enjoy the moment.

41:52.635 --> 41:56.848
You're the one
who made this happen, after all.

41:56.931 --> 41:59.892
You should give yourself
some credit for once.

42:02.478 --> 42:04.147
I don't like it.

42:06.024 --> 42:07.316
What's that?

42:07.400 --> 42:09.402
Got a problem with me,
I'm right here.

42:09.485 --> 42:10.903
That's not what I mean.

42:12.488 --> 42:13.990
The one I'm not happy with...

42:15.783 --> 42:18.995
is myself, for not being able
to just enjoy this moment.

42:24.208 --> 42:26.461
[gulping]

42:26.544 --> 42:28.212
[coughing]

42:28.296 --> 42:29.464
You okay there?

42:29.505 --> 42:30.590
Don't overdo it.

42:30.673 --> 42:32.258
Yamanami's a lightweight,
you know.

42:34.802 --> 42:37.263
Hey, what the hell
is this place?

42:37.346 --> 42:40.808
It's a dump, and it stinks.

42:41.684 --> 42:43.478
Hey.
I hate this.

42:43.519 --> 42:45.313
Who the hell are you?

42:45.354 --> 42:47.523
Hey, hey, hey!

42:47.607 --> 42:48.816
What do you think you're doing,

42:48.900 --> 42:50.777
barging in our dojo
with your shoes on?

42:52.653 --> 42:55.823
Oh, my. Was this supposed
to be a dojo?

42:55.907 --> 42:58.659
It stank so bad,
I thought it was a cesspool.

42:58.701 --> 43:00.369
Why you...
Toshi!

43:00.453 --> 43:01.621
[groans]

43:04.415 --> 43:05.625
Boss...

43:06.918 --> 43:09.754
My sincerest apologies, Sasaki.

43:11.005 --> 43:12.131
How unexpected.

43:12.215 --> 43:14.884
Monkeys have taken up
residence in this cesspit.

43:14.967 --> 43:16.677
Say that again,
you son of a bitch!

43:16.719 --> 43:19.097
Stop it.
That's Sasaki Tadasaburo.

43:19.180 --> 43:21.974
You don't want to mess with him.
[Hijikata] Who the hell is he?

43:22.058 --> 43:24.352
[Nagakura] A grand master
of the Shinto Seibu school.

43:24.393 --> 43:25.978
The finest kodachi user
in all of Japan.

43:26.020 --> 43:27.563
[Yamanami] He's a master
swordsmanship instructor

43:27.647 --> 43:28.564
at the Kobusho.

43:28.648 --> 43:29.565
SASAKI TADASABURO

43:29.649 --> 43:30.858
If we pick a fight,

43:30.942 --> 43:33.778
Kondo's appointment
will be off the table.

43:38.908 --> 43:39.867
And...

43:40.993 --> 43:42.703
what might your business be
with us?

43:42.787 --> 43:44.872
You have a student here

43:44.914 --> 43:49.127
a punk named Saito Hajime,
don't you? Bring him out.

43:50.545 --> 43:53.256
What has our Saito done?

43:53.339 --> 43:55.258
He cut down Ryunosuke,

43:55.341 --> 44:00.763
firstborn son of Hatamoto
Lord Tajima Yamato-no-Kami.

44:07.645 --> 44:11.566
There must be
some kind of mistake.

44:11.649 --> 44:14.443
Yeah, he's right.

44:14.527 --> 44:16.571
Hajime may have
a twisted personality,

44:16.654 --> 44:17.738
but he's no murderer.

44:17.780 --> 44:18.906
Get the hell
out of here.

44:18.948 --> 44:20.700
[Saito]
No, it's not a mistake.

44:25.079 --> 44:29.125
I'm the one who cut down
Tajima Ryunosuke.

44:30.168 --> 44:32.461
[Hijikata, chuckles]
Hey, Hajime.

44:33.754 --> 44:35.715
What's the meaning of this?

44:35.798 --> 44:37.800
I didn't like him,
so I cut him down.

44:37.884 --> 44:39.844
That's all there is to it.

44:50.438 --> 44:52.982
While Kondo is humbling himself
for our sakes,

44:54.275 --> 44:57.278
do you have any idea
what you've just done?

44:58.613 --> 44:59.864
Kondo's...

45:01.157 --> 45:02.867
No...

45:02.950 --> 45:06.245
you're trampling on the dreams
of every single one of us!

45:06.287 --> 45:09.165
Hey, I don't give a damn
about any of that.

45:10.041 --> 45:12.001
I do what I want, when I want.

45:12.084 --> 45:14.253
That's the only rule I live by.

45:18.507 --> 45:19.884
Besides...

45:20.927 --> 45:22.511
I never considered myself

45:22.595 --> 45:24.847
one of your students
to begin with.

45:28.643 --> 45:29.769
Hajime.

45:33.231 --> 45:35.983
[laughing]

45:37.860 --> 45:41.989
You're all just
so damn annoying.

45:42.031 --> 45:45.993
I'm sick and tired of
your little "happy family" act.

45:46.035 --> 45:47.662
[Hijikata]
Hey, Hajime!

45:47.703 --> 45:49.956
Say that again,
you son of a bitch!

45:49.997 --> 45:51.207
[groans]

45:54.669 --> 45:57.838
Let's get the hell out of here,
old man.

46:01.008 --> 46:05.137
Well, that's just the kind
of guy he was.

46:07.223 --> 46:08.933
My condolences.

46:10.726 --> 46:12.353
Hey!

46:14.563 --> 46:15.773
[Okita]
Hijikata!

46:17.900 --> 46:22.530
[♪♪♪]

46:31.789 --> 46:33.082
[Hijikata]
Eisaburo!

46:47.763 --> 46:49.473
You know something,
don't you?

46:54.812 --> 46:56.063
[Kondo]
Why did...

46:56.939 --> 46:59.108
Hajime kill Tajima Ryunosuke?

47:03.321 --> 47:05.948
Me and Hajime...

47:07.783 --> 47:09.952
Before coming to the Shieikan,

47:10.036 --> 47:13.122
we were regulars
at an Itto-ryu dojo.

47:13.205 --> 47:14.457
Ah!

47:17.043 --> 47:17.960
Next!

47:19.462 --> 47:20.463
Hajime!

47:22.631 --> 47:24.133
Ryunosuke.

47:24.216 --> 47:27.011
[Abiru] And Ryunosuke...
he was there, too.

47:34.852 --> 47:35.936
Next!

47:36.020 --> 47:37.938
I'm not done yet!

47:37.980 --> 47:40.858
[Abiru]
Ryunosuke loved swordsmanship;

47:40.941 --> 47:43.319
he just couldn't
get enough of it.

47:46.197 --> 47:47.490
Not yet!

47:53.662 --> 47:55.122
Even though he was frail

47:55.206 --> 47:58.167
and his father
had no faith in him.

47:59.794 --> 48:02.797
Hajime, you are so strong.
Strong!

48:02.880 --> 48:05.132
[laughing]

48:05.174 --> 48:07.301
What are you laughing about?

48:07.385 --> 48:09.929
[Abiru] Even so,
Ryunosuke didn't give up.

48:10.012 --> 48:12.556
He wanted to be strong,
just like Hajime.

48:12.640 --> 48:15.935
Every day, he trained
with that single goal in mind.

48:21.899 --> 48:26.028
But then, the other day...
we received word

48:27.405 --> 48:31.117
that Ryunosuke
has contracted consumption.

48:34.286 --> 48:35.538
I...

48:37.123 --> 48:38.958
I don't have long to live.

48:45.881 --> 48:48.676
Don't make that face.

48:48.759 --> 48:50.428
[chuckling weakly]

48:50.511 --> 48:52.596
[coughing]

49:00.896 --> 49:02.148
Hajime.

49:08.529 --> 49:10.197
I have a favor to ask you.

49:13.784 --> 49:15.119
What is it?

49:16.620 --> 49:17.621
One last time...

49:21.292 --> 49:23.627
I want to face you in a duel
with live blades.

49:27.173 --> 49:30.050
Are you insane?
If you do that, you'll...

49:30.134 --> 49:31.677
I'm going to die anyway!

49:41.312 --> 49:42.271
It's just...

49:44.940 --> 49:46.567
I can't stand it.

49:51.363 --> 49:53.199
To have been born a samurai...

49:55.409 --> 49:58.162
and die having accomplished
nothing.

50:03.626 --> 50:07.254
I want some proof
that I truly lived as a samurai.

50:16.347 --> 50:17.640
Good.

50:27.316 --> 50:30.236
You've always pissed me off.

50:31.654 --> 50:33.280
So before you kick the bucket,

50:33.322 --> 50:35.491
I'm gonna be the one
to kill you.

50:37.826 --> 50:39.203
Hajime...

50:40.329 --> 50:41.789
Stop talking
such nonsense!

50:41.830 --> 50:42.998
We can't fight
each other!

50:43.082 --> 50:44.291
Eisaburo!

50:45.834 --> 50:49.129
Then what the hell do you think
you're training for?

50:49.213 --> 50:52.216
To spend your whole life here
playing at sword fighting?

50:53.926 --> 50:55.344
I'm not.

50:56.845 --> 50:58.389
And neither is Ryunosuke.

50:58.472 --> 51:01.392
[♪♪♪]

51:05.396 --> 51:06.522
Ryunosuke.

51:10.442 --> 51:12.611
Come at me
with everything you've got.

51:22.204 --> 51:24.081
I couldn't stop them.

51:28.419 --> 51:30.588
Because I understood
how Ryunosuke felt.

51:40.055 --> 51:41.432
Is that so...

51:44.935 --> 51:46.937
Where do you think you're going?

51:47.021 --> 51:50.357
I'm going to help Hajime,
what else?

51:52.693 --> 51:54.653
If you go, you're expelled.

51:54.737 --> 51:55.654
Huh?

51:57.448 --> 51:58.407
Why?

51:59.575 --> 52:02.995
All Hajime did was grant
his buddy's final wish!

52:03.078 --> 52:05.122
That doesn't give him
the right to kill.

52:05.205 --> 52:06.498
I know that!

52:09.084 --> 52:10.919
But you remember
what the boss said, right?

52:12.671 --> 52:17.635
"If we eat together and
fight together, we're family."

52:17.718 --> 52:22.014
[Yamanami] Saito killed a man.
That makes him a criminal.

52:22.097 --> 52:24.308
If we help him,
Kondo's appointment

52:24.391 --> 52:26.769
as instructor will be ruined.

52:30.105 --> 52:31.357
Finally...

52:33.192 --> 52:34.985
Finally it's happening.

52:35.069 --> 52:39.073
We've been mocked and dismissed
as country bumpkins with swords.

52:39.114 --> 52:41.241
This is our one chance
to make our name!

52:48.791 --> 52:50.626
Then expel me.

52:54.421 --> 52:56.632
If we can't even protect
our own family...

52:57.966 --> 53:00.803
then what's the point
of making a name for ourselves!

53:13.982 --> 53:15.818
Then expel me, too.

53:20.531 --> 53:23.826
If I lose Hajime too, I...
I won't be able to take it!

53:41.510 --> 53:42.469
Let's go!

54:05.576 --> 54:06.744
Take that!

54:14.960 --> 54:16.211
Is that it?

54:16.295 --> 54:19.757
Doesn't bother me
in the slightest.

54:21.133 --> 54:27.055
Ryunosuke put up
a better fight than this.

54:27.139 --> 54:29.391
Yeah.
If you're going to kill me,

54:29.475 --> 54:31.310
you'd better be serious
about it.

54:40.694 --> 54:41.612
I made you wait.

54:42.654 --> 54:43.572
Lord Tajima.

54:47.409 --> 54:49.453
This is the man, Saito Hajime.

54:49.536 --> 54:54.750
He's your son' s killer.
Please, avenge your son.

54:56.418 --> 54:57.586
Avenge him?

54:59.129 --> 55:00.214
Eh?

55:00.255 --> 55:02.549
For a samurai heir
to be cut down

55:02.633 --> 55:05.385
by some wandering ronin...

55:05.469 --> 55:08.305
is the ultimate disgrace!

55:08.388 --> 55:14.144
Aren't you here
to avenge your son?

55:14.228 --> 55:17.064
This is punishment
for the dishonor

55:17.105 --> 55:18.816
you've brought upon my house.

55:18.899 --> 55:22.486
It's not for a useless whelp
like Ryunosuke.

55:23.529 --> 55:25.364
Fortunately,
my second son, Kotora,

55:25.447 --> 55:26.865
will take over as family head.

55:26.949 --> 55:30.035
Ryunosuke never had
what it takes to be a leader.

55:30.118 --> 55:32.371
You're the real disgrace here.

55:33.455 --> 55:35.541
What did you just say?

55:35.582 --> 55:40.003
[chuckling]
I said you're the disgrace!

55:40.087 --> 55:41.463
[cries out]

55:41.547 --> 55:43.924
You'd better watch your mouth.

55:47.636 --> 55:49.221
Even in the state he was in,

55:49.304 --> 55:51.056
Ryunosuke
managed to land a blow!

55:51.139 --> 55:52.808
He cut me!

55:52.891 --> 55:53.934
Aah!

56:15.539 --> 56:17.958
Is that all you've got?

56:18.000 --> 56:19.418
Hajime...

56:21.461 --> 56:24.798
You're scared to strike me,
aren't you?

56:24.840 --> 56:26.466
Huh?

56:26.508 --> 56:29.636
All you've been doing
is dodging!

56:31.638 --> 56:35.225
You're the one who told me

56:35.309 --> 56:38.145
to come at you
with everything I had!

56:42.941 --> 56:43.942
Is that it?

56:45.027 --> 56:46.987
Hey! Hey!

56:48.947 --> 56:51.950
Is that all the strength
you've got? Ryunosuke!

56:52.034 --> 56:53.994
Ryunosuke! Hey!

56:54.036 --> 56:55.329
[crying out]

56:55.412 --> 56:57.706
Unleash it!
Show me everything you've got!

57:02.920 --> 57:07.049
[♪♪♪]

57:17.768 --> 57:18.894
Thank you.

57:21.355 --> 57:22.731
Hajime.

57:35.744 --> 57:38.622
[Saito]
Ryunosuke was magnificent.

57:39.915 --> 57:42.042
He died with more honor
as a samurai

57:42.084 --> 57:44.920
than a piece of shit
like you ever will.

57:48.423 --> 57:52.678
Shut your filthy mouth,
you maggot.

57:52.761 --> 57:54.763
[groans]

57:56.098 --> 57:57.182
[fighting nearby]

57:57.265 --> 57:58.642
[retainer]
Who are you?

58:00.602 --> 58:02.604
[Hijikata sighs]

58:03.438 --> 58:05.941
[Sasaki]
Oh my! Welcome.

58:06.024 --> 58:10.737
Don't get the wrong idea.
I'm not here to save him.

58:12.572 --> 58:14.449
I'm the strongest man in Edo.

58:14.533 --> 58:16.952
You think
I can just let that slide?

58:17.035 --> 58:19.037
Who the hell are you?

58:20.455 --> 58:22.916
Who the hell are they?
Please stand back.

58:24.710 --> 58:28.964
We will dispose
of these annoying flies.

58:33.468 --> 58:35.512
Only two people
showed up to help?

58:35.595 --> 58:37.556
You're not very popular,
are you?

58:37.639 --> 58:39.850
You idiot.
What are you doing here?

58:39.933 --> 58:41.435
You are the real idiot,
Hajime!

58:41.518 --> 58:43.228
Trying to take this all
on yourself.

58:43.311 --> 58:45.188
[Saito]
Just get out of here, now!

58:45.272 --> 58:46.273
Hajime!

58:58.660 --> 59:00.787
So, how do you wanna die?

59:01.955 --> 59:03.040
Huh?

59:05.125 --> 59:06.084
Me? My wish is to die

59:06.168 --> 59:08.837
fighting a strong opponent
with all I have.

59:10.714 --> 59:14.051
I'll bet that Ryunosuke kid
felt the same way.

59:14.134 --> 59:16.678
[♪♪♪]

59:26.354 --> 59:28.690
[shouts fiercely]

59:32.360 --> 59:33.320
Bring it.

59:34.654 --> 59:36.198
[laughing]

59:42.579 --> 59:44.039
Full of spirit, aren't you?

59:46.124 --> 59:47.250
I like that.

59:49.503 --> 59:50.837
Stay out of this.

59:52.547 --> 59:53.882
This one's mine.

59:55.050 --> 59:56.009
Bring it on!

01:00:10.398 --> 01:00:11.608
Ouch!

01:00:11.691 --> 01:00:14.611
[straining]

01:00:34.256 --> 01:00:35.298
Guess I have no choice.

01:00:37.676 --> 01:00:38.927
Time to settle this!

01:00:48.770 --> 01:00:49.938
Hiraseigan...

01:00:52.065 --> 01:00:52.983
You...

01:00:54.317 --> 01:00:55.902
intend to die here?

01:01:00.365 --> 01:01:01.658
Fine by me.

01:01:03.618 --> 01:01:05.453
I admire that spirit.

01:01:08.623 --> 01:01:10.250
Tennen Rishin-ryu:
Sword of No Light!

01:01:13.086 --> 01:01:15.589
Looks like things
are heating up!

01:01:15.630 --> 01:01:17.591
Let me get in on the action!

01:01:17.674 --> 01:01:19.176
Boss!

01:01:19.259 --> 01:01:21.845
Crashing the party!

01:01:21.928 --> 01:01:25.599
[chuckling] What the?
Did everyone end up coming?

01:01:25.640 --> 01:01:27.100
This isn't some casual
get-together.

01:01:27.184 --> 01:01:29.811
A festival is for everyone
to enjoy, right?

01:01:29.895 --> 01:01:31.313
[chuckles softly]

01:01:34.441 --> 01:01:37.444
So he's not coming after all?

01:01:37.485 --> 01:01:38.445
Boss...

01:01:41.114 --> 01:01:44.242
What the hell
do you think you're doing?

01:01:44.326 --> 01:01:47.370
You son of a bitch! I'm not
your student or anything else!

01:01:47.454 --> 01:01:49.247
Didn't I already tell you that?

01:01:51.333 --> 01:01:52.751
Hajime!

01:01:53.960 --> 01:01:56.254
You're right.
You're not my student.

01:02:15.941 --> 01:02:17.192
You're my precious...

01:02:19.694 --> 01:02:21.321
family.

01:02:21.404 --> 01:02:24.199
[♪♪♪]

01:02:31.373 --> 01:02:32.832
[Abiru]
Yamanami?

01:02:37.379 --> 01:02:38.296
What gives?

01:02:39.923 --> 01:02:42.050
I thought helping
meant expulsion.

01:02:43.760 --> 01:02:46.054
It's against my better judgment,
but...

01:02:46.137 --> 01:02:48.473
but I cannot defy
the dojo master.

01:02:50.600 --> 01:02:52.227
[laughing]

01:02:58.233 --> 01:02:59.985
All right.

01:03:01.945 --> 01:03:03.571
Now everyone's here.

01:03:05.699 --> 01:03:07.075
Let's settle this.

01:03:08.410 --> 01:03:09.411
Please wait a moment

01:03:11.162 --> 01:03:12.080
Lord Tajima.

01:03:17.460 --> 01:03:19.045
Would you please look at this?

01:03:27.095 --> 01:03:29.097
It's a note left by your son.

01:03:31.266 --> 01:03:33.059
Why do you have this?

01:03:33.101 --> 01:03:36.604
Your wife found it
and brought it to me.

01:03:36.688 --> 01:03:38.898
It says here that your son

01:03:38.982 --> 01:03:43.153
intends to face this man
in a duel.

01:03:47.365 --> 01:03:50.535
This was entirely
your son's decision.

01:03:53.038 --> 01:03:55.123
If you still refuse
to back down...

01:03:57.000 --> 01:03:58.543
then we accept your challenge.

01:04:00.253 --> 01:04:03.965
Look at all the flies
buzzing around.

01:04:04.049 --> 01:04:06.301
God, how annoying.

01:04:09.095 --> 01:04:11.139
I'm gonna kill
every last one of you!

01:04:11.973 --> 01:04:14.100
That's enough! Stop!

01:04:18.730 --> 01:04:19.939
Let's go.

01:04:26.071 --> 01:04:27.113
Kondo.

01:04:28.865 --> 01:04:32.202
That's the end
of your Kobusho appointment.

01:04:44.005 --> 01:04:45.382
It can't be helped.

01:04:47.342 --> 01:04:50.011
All this for a stray dog
like him?

01:04:50.095 --> 01:04:51.679
What a bunch of weirdos.

01:04:56.434 --> 01:04:57.477
Let's go.

01:04:57.519 --> 01:04:58.478
Sir.

01:05:10.949 --> 01:05:12.158
Hajime.

01:05:20.500 --> 01:05:22.335
Ouch!

01:05:23.545 --> 01:05:25.713
[Saito groaning]

01:05:25.797 --> 01:05:26.965
You did well!

01:05:27.048 --> 01:05:29.342
[Saito]
That hurts. Boss, that hurts.

01:05:37.392 --> 01:05:38.643
[laughs]

01:05:38.726 --> 01:05:40.562
[laughs]

01:05:42.730 --> 01:05:45.692
[♪♪♪]

01:06:16.139 --> 01:06:18.349
[Hijikata] Hajime, where do you
think you're going?

01:06:26.524 --> 01:06:30.278
Thanks to everyone, they've
agreed not to press charges.

01:06:33.907 --> 01:06:35.283
Whatever the reason...

01:06:37.535 --> 01:06:39.746
I still killed a man.

01:06:39.787 --> 01:06:41.664
I can't just pretend
it never happened.

01:06:47.962 --> 01:06:49.255
I've caused...

01:06:51.341 --> 01:06:53.301
Boss and everyone
so much trouble.

01:07:01.768 --> 01:07:03.520
You're such an awkward man.

01:07:05.146 --> 01:07:07.232
I don't want to hear that
from you.

01:07:10.985 --> 01:07:12.320
See ya.

01:07:20.286 --> 01:07:24.165
[Nagakura] Hajime would later
change his name to Fujita Goro.

01:07:24.249 --> 01:07:26.543
The Fujita family's records
are said

01:07:26.626 --> 01:07:28.002
to state the following:

01:07:28.086 --> 01:07:31.422
"Saito Hajime,
in his late teens,

01:07:31.506 --> 01:07:35.134
killed a man
and was forced to leave Edo."

01:07:37.178 --> 01:07:39.389
THREE YEARS LATER

01:07:41.057 --> 01:07:42.892
That year, to coincide
with the 14th Shogun

01:07:42.976 --> 01:07:45.979
Iemochi's procession to Kyoto

01:07:46.062 --> 01:07:49.857
the Roshigumi was formed
to serve as his escort.

01:07:49.941 --> 01:07:52.986
Its ranks were filled
with ronin,

01:07:53.069 --> 01:07:55.405
farmers, and even criminals.

01:07:55.488 --> 01:07:58.366
Skilled fighters
from all walks of life.

01:08:00.285 --> 01:08:04.872
And we of the Shieikan dojo
decided to join their ranks.

01:08:06.165 --> 01:08:07.792
[Nagakura]
I gotta say, though.

01:08:07.875 --> 01:08:12.547
I never thought we'd be in Kyo,
protecting the Shogun himself.

01:08:12.630 --> 01:08:16.175
We'll eventually become hatamoto
for the Shogun, right?

01:08:16.216 --> 01:08:19.554
Talk about moving up
in the world!

01:08:19.636 --> 01:08:22.307
Hey, Yamanami.
I was just thinking...

01:08:22.390 --> 01:08:26.644
Why's the Shogun
going to Kyoto anyway?

01:08:26.728 --> 01:08:28.979
[Yamanami]
The Imperial Court summoned him

01:08:29.063 --> 01:08:31.691
to pressure him
to expel the foreigners.

01:08:31.733 --> 01:08:33.234
Since the Black Ships arrived,

01:08:33.318 --> 01:08:35.694
the Shogunate's power
has been declining.

01:08:37.363 --> 01:08:40.325
Basically, the Tokugawa
are losing their grip.

01:08:43.368 --> 01:08:47.957
This is a once-in-a-lifetime
opportunity for us!

01:08:48.041 --> 01:08:50.417
Kyo is now the heart of Japan!

01:08:52.377 --> 01:08:54.881
To test their skills

01:08:54.964 --> 01:08:58.134
they say the most famous
swordsmen have gathered there.

01:08:59.636 --> 01:09:00.720
Listen up, everyone!

01:09:04.765 --> 01:09:06.434
We'll win glory in Kyo

01:09:07.518 --> 01:09:09.354
and let the name of the Shieikan

01:09:11.773 --> 01:09:13.649
be known across the land!

01:09:13.733 --> 01:09:15.318
Bring it on! Let's do it!

01:09:15.401 --> 01:09:17.236
[all shouting excitedly]

01:09:17.319 --> 01:09:20.448
[♪♪♪]

01:09:26.120 --> 01:09:27.455
Hm.

01:09:31.292 --> 01:09:33.461
[baby crying]

01:09:37.048 --> 01:09:38.758
[dog barking]

01:09:40.385 --> 01:09:42.428
So this is Kyo, huh?

01:09:43.720 --> 01:09:45.598
It's pretty run-down.

01:09:45.640 --> 01:09:48.350
I thought this was
supposed to be the capital.

01:09:49.560 --> 01:09:52.313
This is a lot different
from what I'd heard.

01:09:54.482 --> 01:09:56.234
"A lot" is an understatement.

01:10:02.782 --> 01:10:04.784
I am Kiyokawa Hachiro!

01:10:07.078 --> 01:10:08.454
Gentlemen!

01:10:09.497 --> 01:10:11.541
This Roshigumi was formed

01:10:11.624 --> 01:10:15.503
to escort the Shogun
on his procession to Kyoto.

01:10:16.671 --> 01:10:17.630
However!

01:10:19.006 --> 01:10:20.883
The Shogunate

01:10:20.967 --> 01:10:24.804
is now nothing but a sinking
ship, headed for ruin!

01:10:24.846 --> 01:10:26.639
[murmuring]

01:10:28.349 --> 01:10:31.227
From this day forward,

01:10:31.310 --> 01:10:33.938
we serve
as the Emperor's personal guard

01:10:34.021 --> 01:10:38.693
protect the Imperial Court,
and expel the barbarians!

01:10:40.611 --> 01:10:42.488
That is the true calling...

01:10:43.364 --> 01:10:45.491
of those loyal to the Emperor!

01:10:45.575 --> 01:10:46.993
What the hell
is he talking about?

01:10:47.076 --> 01:10:48.035
From now on...

01:10:48.119 --> 01:10:49.412
It seems we've been had.

01:10:49.495 --> 01:10:50.747
...our mission is no longer...

01:10:50.830 --> 01:10:53.833
We've been had?
...to guard the Shogun...

01:10:53.916 --> 01:10:58.337
Kiyokawa intends to use us
to expel foreigners,

01:10:58.379 --> 01:11:00.506
not to guard the Shogun.

01:11:00.590 --> 01:11:03.509
But that's treason
against the Shogunate!

01:11:03.551 --> 01:11:05.803
Rise for the Emperor!
Is that true?

01:11:07.638 --> 01:11:10.183
Now is the time
to expel the foreigners!

01:11:10.266 --> 01:11:12.351
We'll return to Edo!

01:11:12.435 --> 01:11:15.938
Edo? Hey! We just got to Kyo!

01:11:16.022 --> 01:11:17.690
He's right!

01:11:17.732 --> 01:11:19.901
Ouch!
What the hell is your problem?

01:11:19.984 --> 01:11:21.694
Hey, hold it right there.

01:11:21.736 --> 01:11:25.490
Sorry.
I'm talking to you, you bastard!

01:11:26.407 --> 01:11:28.534
A fight?
Toshi! Toshi!

01:11:28.576 --> 01:11:32.705
You're gonna bump into me
and not say a damn thing?

01:11:32.789 --> 01:11:34.499
You trying to pick a fight
with me,

01:11:34.582 --> 01:11:36.000
Araki of Reconnaissance Squad?

01:11:37.168 --> 01:11:38.252
Ha!

01:11:38.336 --> 01:11:40.087
Cat got your tongue?

01:11:40.171 --> 01:11:41.923
[laughing]

01:11:42.924 --> 01:11:44.759
[gagging]

01:11:47.637 --> 01:11:51.724
That was close... I almost puked
all the sake I drank yesterday.

01:11:54.227 --> 01:11:56.604
Huh? And who the hell are you?

01:11:57.688 --> 01:11:58.856
You bastard!

01:12:00.274 --> 01:12:01.734
You're dead!

01:12:01.818 --> 01:12:04.529
I like this.
Pure, unhesitating violence.

01:12:09.909 --> 01:12:11.619
[groaning, gasping]

01:12:11.702 --> 01:12:14.622
I love the energy.
Man, I feel sick.

01:12:14.705 --> 01:12:18.835
You lot! What do you think
you're doing? Halt!

01:12:27.552 --> 01:12:29.846
You're from Mito, aren't you?

01:12:29.929 --> 01:12:31.472
What of it?

01:12:31.556 --> 01:12:34.141
I was very impressed
by the Mito ronin

01:12:34.225 --> 01:12:36.102
at the Sakuradamon Incident.

01:12:36.185 --> 01:12:37.353
It bolstered my resolve

01:12:37.436 --> 01:12:39.230
to revere the Emperor
and expel them.

01:12:39.313 --> 01:12:42.358
They must be your comrades, too.

01:12:42.441 --> 01:12:44.986
Don't you wish to change
the course of history,

01:12:45.069 --> 01:12:46.279
guided by that same will?

01:12:46.362 --> 01:12:48.114
Nah, not interested.

01:12:48.197 --> 01:12:50.283
[chuckles]

01:12:50.366 --> 01:12:51.450
I'm not going back to Edo.

01:12:51.492 --> 01:12:53.744
I haven't even
gotten laid today.

01:12:53.828 --> 01:12:57.665
You bastard! How dare you mock
Master Kiyokawa! Unforgivable!

01:13:02.879 --> 01:13:03.880
That's enough!

01:13:06.841 --> 01:13:07.758
Hey...

01:13:09.594 --> 01:13:11.637
Draw your sword, Kiyokawa!

01:13:11.679 --> 01:13:18.603
If it's kill or be killed,
let's go all the way! Right?

01:13:22.815 --> 01:13:24.317
That's enough!

01:13:24.358 --> 01:13:25.902
Huh?

01:13:27.194 --> 01:13:28.195
Get lost.

01:13:29.989 --> 01:13:31.657
[groans]

01:13:31.741 --> 01:13:33.743
Man. You killed the mood.

01:13:35.077 --> 01:13:41.083
Dammit. What a total buzzkill.
Such a buzzkill.

01:13:42.668 --> 01:13:44.420
Oh well, nothing to be done.

01:13:44.503 --> 01:13:46.297
All right,
off to Shimabara with you.

01:13:46.380 --> 01:13:47.840
Wait!

01:13:47.924 --> 01:13:49.175
[Serizawa]
Huh?

01:13:50.968 --> 01:13:54.013
[♪♪♪]

01:13:55.890 --> 01:13:57.350
Who the hell are you?

01:13:57.391 --> 01:14:00.227
You first. Right?

01:14:00.311 --> 01:14:01.562
When you ask for a name,

01:14:01.646 --> 01:14:03.940
isn't it polite
to give your own first?

01:14:05.483 --> 01:14:07.777
Right?
Hijikata Toshizo.

01:14:08.861 --> 01:14:09.987
What?

01:14:10.071 --> 01:14:13.366
Hijikata Toshizo!

01:14:13.407 --> 01:14:15.534
[laughing]

01:14:15.576 --> 01:14:19.830
Well now, how interesting.
Ah, I see, I see.

01:14:24.335 --> 01:14:25.753
I'm Serizawa Kamo.

01:14:26.963 --> 01:14:29.423
Favorite word: "Violence."
That's the name.

01:14:29.507 --> 01:14:31.258
[sniffs]
Later.

01:14:35.388 --> 01:14:37.556
Serizawa Kamo...

01:14:37.598 --> 01:14:41.268
[♪♪♪]

01:14:41.352 --> 01:14:44.689
[Hijikata]
Man, you gotta love Kyo.

01:14:44.730 --> 01:14:46.691
If I can scrap with crazy guys
like that,

01:14:46.732 --> 01:14:49.527
then the trip here
was more than worth it.

01:14:49.610 --> 01:14:51.904
But what're we gonna do?

01:14:51.946 --> 01:14:55.241
Kiyokawa's planning
to go back to Edo, right?

01:14:55.324 --> 01:14:56.784
Are we going back, too?

01:14:58.244 --> 01:14:59.912
It's not that simple.

01:14:59.996 --> 01:15:00.913
Huh?

01:15:00.997 --> 01:15:03.082
You don't agree
with the expulsionists?

01:15:04.458 --> 01:15:06.711
There's a more pressing issue.

01:15:06.794 --> 01:15:09.797
Whether we head to Edo
or remain here in Kyo

01:15:10.798 --> 01:15:13.509
we're short on funds.

01:15:13.592 --> 01:15:16.846
What the hell?
Hey, what're you talking about?

01:15:18.431 --> 01:15:20.433
I was a fool to think things
would work out

01:15:20.516 --> 01:15:22.184
once we reached the capital.

01:15:23.894 --> 01:15:26.063
Don't beat yourself up over it.

01:15:26.147 --> 01:15:29.191
There's a right and wrong way
to make a name for yourself.

01:15:29.275 --> 01:15:32.069
And I don't like Kiyokawa's way
of deceiving people.

01:15:33.529 --> 01:15:35.990
We'll just make a name
for ourselves our own way.

01:15:43.456 --> 01:15:45.708
In that case...
First things first,

01:15:45.791 --> 01:15:47.001
we need to earn our keep.

01:15:47.084 --> 01:15:51.172
Yeah. If we can't,
we'll starve in a ditch.

01:15:51.255 --> 01:15:53.007
This is where the fun starts.

01:15:55.801 --> 01:15:59.013
Please, I'm begging you.

01:15:59.096 --> 01:16:01.140
For days, men calling for
the expulsion of foreigners

01:16:01.182 --> 01:16:05.311
have been attacking anyone
with ties to the shogunate!

01:16:05.352 --> 01:16:08.689
I said get out. Now leave.

01:16:08.773 --> 01:16:10.858
Why should I have to hire

01:16:10.941 --> 01:16:14.153
a bunch of nobodies
from the sticks?

01:16:19.950 --> 01:16:21.744
What the hell?

01:16:21.827 --> 01:16:24.789
You think being a hatamoto
makes you so damn special?

01:16:26.290 --> 01:16:27.666
Damn it!

01:16:29.210 --> 01:16:31.128
So, we've been turned away
at the gate again.

01:16:33.047 --> 01:16:35.966
Why do you have to grovel
like that to them, Kondo?

01:16:38.552 --> 01:16:40.096
There is no use in rushing.

01:16:41.180 --> 01:16:43.557
Our funds will only last
three more days.

01:16:43.641 --> 01:16:46.102
We must find work
before then.

01:16:50.272 --> 01:16:51.607
Sorry.

01:16:53.901 --> 01:16:56.278
[music playing,
indistinct singing]

01:16:56.362 --> 01:16:57.404
Huh?

01:16:59.240 --> 01:17:05.538
ROSHIGUMI QUARTERS

01:17:05.579 --> 01:17:06.789
[laughter]

01:17:06.872 --> 01:17:12.211
Delicious! I'm so happy!

01:17:12.253 --> 01:17:15.756
Hey! You aren't eating at all!
What are you doing?

01:17:21.345 --> 01:17:23.722
What the hell do you guys think
you're doing?

01:17:23.764 --> 01:17:25.474
Appreciate you stoppin' by!

01:17:25.558 --> 01:17:26.725
What is all this?

01:17:26.767 --> 01:17:29.687
We have been exerting ourselves
greatly.

01:17:29.770 --> 01:17:33.232
Calm down.
C'mon, have some of this.

01:17:33.274 --> 01:17:36.569
Kamo's treatin' tonight.

01:17:36.652 --> 01:17:37.820
Kamo?

01:17:37.903 --> 01:17:39.989
This guy, right here.
You know him, right?

01:17:41.657 --> 01:17:43.784
Serizawa.
Hm?

01:17:43.868 --> 01:17:47.413
Oh, my. You're quite a large man
yourself.

01:17:47.496 --> 01:17:49.582
So you're the commander,
Kondo Isami?

01:17:49.623 --> 01:17:51.000
I've heard the rumors.

01:17:51.083 --> 01:17:52.001
I'm honored.

01:17:53.460 --> 01:17:58.215
Still... this is just what
I'd expect from you, Serizawa.

01:17:58.299 --> 01:18:01.010
It must be nice
to have such deep pockets.

01:18:01.093 --> 01:18:03.262
[chuckling]

01:18:03.304 --> 01:18:07.766
Nah, I ain't got any money.

01:18:07.808 --> 01:18:10.269
[Hijikata] What?
Not a penny.

01:18:10.352 --> 01:18:11.478
What?
None.

01:18:11.562 --> 01:18:13.189
[chuckling]
What are you saying?

01:18:13.272 --> 01:18:14.231
Oh!

01:18:16.525 --> 01:18:18.110
Hey, what? What?

01:18:20.613 --> 01:18:21.822
What's wrong?

01:18:23.073 --> 01:18:27.286
This pouch...
It had all of our money in it.

01:18:27.328 --> 01:18:28.996
There was something in there.

01:18:35.961 --> 01:18:38.797
You son of a bitch!
You played us for fools!

01:18:38.839 --> 01:18:40.424
Want a piece of me? huh?

01:18:42.885 --> 01:18:44.803
That just means you're a moron.

01:18:44.887 --> 01:18:46.430
[Hijikata]
Hey!

01:18:46.513 --> 01:18:49.183
You've got a hell
of a lot of nerve. You bastard!

01:18:51.727 --> 01:18:53.354
You want a piece of me, asshole?

01:18:54.688 --> 01:18:56.315
[claps]

01:18:57.274 --> 01:18:58.943
[laughing]

01:19:00.819 --> 01:19:03.155
Knock it off. That's enough.

01:19:03.239 --> 01:19:06.867
You all had your fun,
didn't you?

01:19:06.951 --> 01:19:08.452
Can't really complain now.

01:19:10.663 --> 01:19:13.290
Right, Serizawa?

01:19:16.252 --> 01:19:19.922
Nah, I don't think
they have to stop.

01:19:20.005 --> 01:19:22.341
Flowers, women,
and booze are fine,

01:19:22.383 --> 01:19:24.301
but isn't something missing?

01:19:25.636 --> 01:19:26.762
After all, the one thing

01:19:26.845 --> 01:19:28.722
that really gets
a man's blood pumping...

01:19:28.806 --> 01:19:31.517
is good old-fashioned violence.
Ain't that right?

01:19:33.102 --> 01:19:37.481
Kamo, you're a real piece
of work, you know that?

01:19:37.564 --> 01:19:38.983
How about you and me have a go?

01:19:39.066 --> 01:19:41.068
Mm...

01:19:43.362 --> 01:19:45.155
No, you don't do it for me.

01:19:46.532 --> 01:19:47.449
[snorts]

01:19:50.035 --> 01:19:51.203
Right...

01:20:00.170 --> 01:20:01.588
[coughs]

01:20:14.101 --> 01:20:18.105
I'll take you on instead,
Kondo.

01:20:23.944 --> 01:20:27.698
For now, let's just
call it a night.

01:20:27.781 --> 01:20:30.034
What the hell?
Talk about an anticlimax.

01:20:30.075 --> 01:20:32.036
Kondo Isami
of the Tennen Rishin style,

01:20:32.077 --> 01:20:34.663
turning tail and running.
I guess it's nothing

01:20:34.747 --> 01:20:36.665
but a farmer's hick sword style
in the end.

01:20:36.749 --> 01:20:38.083
Cut the crap!

01:20:38.167 --> 01:20:40.586
Right.
And I hear your Shieikan dojo

01:20:40.627 --> 01:20:43.630
is a cesspit
full of insolent thugs.

01:20:43.714 --> 01:20:44.798
No wonder it stinks.

01:20:44.882 --> 01:20:46.050
[Hijikata]
You son of a bitch!

01:20:46.133 --> 01:20:47.843
[Okita]
Insult Kondo again and I'll...

01:20:48.969 --> 01:20:50.304
Cut you down.

01:20:50.387 --> 01:20:51.472
[Serizawa]
Huh?

01:20:53.640 --> 01:20:57.186
Yeah? You gonna try and cut me
down? Can you do that?

01:20:59.396 --> 01:21:02.566
I don't know the meaning
of holding back.

01:21:02.649 --> 01:21:04.151
It's fine.

01:21:04.234 --> 01:21:07.237
I'm not very good
at that myself.

01:21:07.321 --> 01:21:09.573
[chuckles]
I like this kid. You got guts.

01:21:12.409 --> 01:21:15.204
You drew your blade.
This is a duel to the death.

01:21:17.623 --> 01:21:19.041
Wouldn't have it any other way.

01:21:19.124 --> 01:21:22.419
Oume, you just wait right there.

01:21:29.510 --> 01:21:31.136
Ooh...!

01:21:31.178 --> 01:21:34.598
If that's the best you can do,
you're a dead man.

01:21:34.681 --> 01:21:36.934
[laughs]

01:21:37.017 --> 01:21:40.062
Don't you underestimate me, boy.

01:21:40.145 --> 01:21:44.691
I've never seen Soji
look like that.

01:21:44.775 --> 01:21:46.026
Ah...

01:21:46.110 --> 01:21:50.155
Those eyes... I see. I see now.

01:21:50.239 --> 01:21:53.200
You are on this side too...

01:21:56.328 --> 01:21:57.454
Bring it on!

01:22:08.257 --> 01:22:09.591
Awesome.

01:22:22.729 --> 01:22:24.314
I like it.

01:22:26.024 --> 01:22:28.110
[chuckling]

01:23:00.684 --> 01:23:05.063
Man, it's hot.

01:23:05.105 --> 01:23:08.066
This place is way too cramped.

01:23:10.611 --> 01:23:11.904
[sighs]

01:23:11.945 --> 01:23:13.405
It's nice out here.

01:23:17.242 --> 01:23:19.077
Flowers and violence.

01:23:23.290 --> 01:23:25.209
Okay, okay. I like it.

01:24:08.293 --> 01:24:13.215
Yeah, this is a rush.

01:24:14.174 --> 01:24:16.301
You're still so green.

01:24:17.594 --> 01:24:20.305
Don't push yourself...
your head's spinning, right?

01:24:20.347 --> 01:24:23.850
Serizawa! You are a coward,
you bastard!

01:24:26.144 --> 01:24:27.479
Fine by me.

01:24:28.689 --> 01:24:31.108
There's no honor
or cowardice in violence.

01:24:38.156 --> 01:24:40.367
The cherry blossoms...
they're falling.

01:24:44.830 --> 01:24:46.373
Hm...

01:24:53.255 --> 01:24:55.215
Finally took the bait, huh?

01:24:56.383 --> 01:24:58.635
Pull back
and you'll lose a finger.

01:25:03.056 --> 01:25:04.391
Soji...

01:25:06.893 --> 01:25:07.811
lost.

01:25:10.564 --> 01:25:11.815
As for his life...

01:25:16.403 --> 01:25:18.739
Consider it a debt to me.

01:25:25.912 --> 01:25:27.164
No.

01:25:28.415 --> 01:25:31.793
We're even. I had my fun.

01:25:42.137 --> 01:25:43.889
Now there's a man.

01:25:45.432 --> 01:25:50.437
[sighing] Damn, what a buzzkill.
Sobered me right up.

01:26:02.908 --> 01:26:04.159
[Todo]
Boss's hand!

01:26:06.578 --> 01:26:07.663
Okita!

01:26:18.006 --> 01:26:18.965
Kondo.

01:26:21.760 --> 01:26:22.844
I'm sorry.

01:26:24.971 --> 01:26:25.972
Next time...

01:26:29.101 --> 01:26:30.477
No...

01:26:33.772 --> 01:26:39.903
I swear...
I'll never lose to anyone again.

01:26:41.321 --> 01:26:44.825
[Kondo] That's enough, Soji.
You're all right.

01:26:49.830 --> 01:26:50.872
[sighs]

01:26:50.956 --> 01:26:52.499
[Okita sobbing]

01:26:52.582 --> 01:26:53.625
You're okay now.

01:26:55.669 --> 01:26:58.588
[♪♪♪]

01:27:22.154 --> 01:27:23.530
[Hijikata]
How's Soji?

01:27:25.282 --> 01:27:26.575
He's calmed down.

01:27:27.659 --> 01:27:29.745
His head injury
wasn't anything serious.

01:27:33.749 --> 01:27:34.708
Good.

01:27:45.510 --> 01:27:47.971
"There's no honor or cowardice
in violence," huh?

01:27:53.226 --> 01:27:54.728
That's Serizawa for you.

01:27:58.690 --> 01:28:00.901
I've said
similar things myself.

01:28:04.571 --> 01:28:06.740
But...
Serizawa and I are different.

01:28:10.202 --> 01:28:12.579
That man knows
what a real battle is.

01:28:19.878 --> 01:28:22.589
A man like that...
he's most terrifying.

01:28:29.721 --> 01:28:31.973
Before I knew it,
my hands were shaking.

01:28:38.647 --> 01:28:39.689
And yet...

01:28:43.109 --> 01:28:44.945
I'm dying to fight him.

01:28:49.199 --> 01:28:50.617
Stupid, isn't it?

01:28:52.619 --> 01:28:54.913
Especially with what Soji
just went through.

01:29:08.093 --> 01:29:09.636
You're an idiot,
all right.

01:29:11.930 --> 01:29:12.848
But...

01:29:17.727 --> 01:29:19.938
I'm excited
to see what you'll become.

01:29:21.648 --> 01:29:23.692
One who knows oneself
grows strong.

01:29:25.318 --> 01:29:27.070
So does one
who has known defeat.

01:29:29.447 --> 01:29:34.744
[♪♪♪]

01:29:34.786 --> 01:29:35.954
[chuckles softly]

01:29:38.498 --> 01:29:40.166
Knowing defeat, huh?

01:29:43.336 --> 01:29:44.880
I don't wanna lose.

01:30:37.223 --> 01:30:38.600
[Nagakura] In those days,

01:30:38.683 --> 01:30:41.645
the heart of Japan
was the capital, Kyo.

01:30:41.686 --> 01:30:42.896
[sighs]

01:30:45.190 --> 01:30:47.400
[exclaims]
[groans]

01:30:47.484 --> 01:30:50.445
Samurai
confident in their skill

01:30:50.528 --> 01:30:54.366
flocked to the city
to test their mettle.

01:30:54.407 --> 01:30:56.576
[dog barking]

01:30:58.578 --> 01:31:00.080
[blood gushing]

01:31:00.163 --> 01:31:03.792
Among them was a man
once called a friend.

01:31:06.753 --> 01:31:10.799
You bastard! You're a manslayer!

01:31:10.882 --> 01:31:12.092
[yells fiercely]

01:31:13.301 --> 01:31:15.095
[gurgles, gasps]

01:31:15.178 --> 01:31:19.391
DIVINE RETRIBUTION

01:31:19.432 --> 01:31:23.895
[♪♪♪]

01:31:23.937 --> 01:31:25.855
Before we knew it,

01:31:25.939 --> 01:31:29.818
we were swept
into a whirlwind of upheaval.

01:31:34.030 --> 01:31:36.616
[♪♪♪]

01:31:41.121 --> 01:31:42.288
[grunting]

01:32:10.150 --> 01:32:13.069
[♪♪♪]

01:32:49.522 --> 01:32:52.692
[♪♪♪]

01:33:25.391 --> 01:33:29.729
[Yoshiaki Dewa's "Chiruran
Shinsengumi Requiem" playing]
